    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10202" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">confrăgus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		confringo (post-Aug.; <b>poet.</b> for
		confragosus), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>rough, rugged, uneven</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dumeta densis arboribus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					6, 126</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Val.
				Fl. 3, 581</span></i>.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">con-frăga</span></b> , ōrum,
			n., <i>a rough place, thicket</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">silvae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 4, 494</span></i>
			.—<i>Comp., sup.</i>, and
			adv. not in use.</div>
